==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-all in all.ogg|a=AU}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|modal|set phrase}} [[generally|Generally]], [[all things considered]]
#: {{ux|en|'''All in all''', it's not a bad little restaurant.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=April|author=Stirling Everard|title=A Matter of Pedigree|journal=Railway Magazine|issue=600|page=273|text=There are, of course, certain differences of detail; for example, the placing of the safety valves on the boiler barrel behind the dome, which follows the practice in the Riddles 2-8-0 and 2-10-0 locomotives for the Ministry of Supply; but taken '''all in all''', ''Britannia's'' boiler has a closer affinity with the Doncaster designs than with any other.}}
# [[altogether|Altogether]], [[in all]], with [[everything]] [[included]]
#: {{ux|en|There were twenty absentees '''all in all'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[altogether|Altogether]], [[wholly]], in every [[way]]
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XIV|23|And I perceived no touch of change,<br>⁠No hint of death in all his frame,<br>⁠But found him '''all in all''' the same, […]}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|generally}} {{l|en|for the most part}}, {{l|en|mostly}}, {{l|en|on the whole}}; see also [[Thesaurus:mostly]]

