===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Everything that matters; the only thing of importance.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1822|author=[[w:William Goode, the elder|William Goode]]|title=Essays on all the scriptural names and titles of Christ|page=181
|passage={{...}} to realize, by constant faith, the all-sufficiency of his redeeming power and love &mdash; to make him all his salvation and all his desire, the Alpha and Omega of all his hope, his '''all in all'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Vanity Fair|passage=You saw us all in happier days before he married me. I was '''all in all''' then to him; or would he have given up his fortune, his family, as he nobly did to make me happy?}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1828|author=Constantine Henry Phipps Marquess of Normanby|title=Yes and No: a Tale of the Day|page=12|passage=Her mother had been '''all in all''' to her: she had never seemed to have any separate existence from that of her child.}}

